{"strongs": "H5697", "word": "עֶגְלָה", "translit": "eg.lah", "root": "עגל", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun feminine", "gloss": "heifer", "definition": "I. עֶגְלָה noun feminine heifer ; — absolute ׳ ע Gen 15:9 +; construct עֶגְלַת Isa 7:21 +; suffix עֶגְלָתִי Judg 14:18 plural construct עֶגְלוֺת Hos 10:5 (but see below); — heifer , Isa 7:21 , used in ploughing Judg 14:18 (figurative), threshing Jer 50:11 ( דָשָׁא ׳ ע , in simile, see דּוּשׁ , read perhaps דָשָׁה ), figurative of stateliness etc. Jer 46:20 מְלֻמָּדָה ׳ ע Hos 10:11 a trained heifer (simile of Ephraim); used for sacrifice 1Sam 16:2 ( עֶגְלַת בָּקָר ); cut in two for ratifying covenant Gen 15:9 ( J ; מְשֻׁלֶּשֶׁת ׳ ע ; compare עֵגֶל Jer 34:18 ; Jer 34:19 ); in cleansing city from blood-guiltiness Deut 21:3 ( בָּקָר ׳ ע ), v Deut 21:4 v Deut 21:4 v Deut 21:6 once of calves worshipped in Northern Israel Hos 10:5 (where read probably עֵגֶל , so ᵐ5 We Now GASm , compare Che , see also the following suffixes masculine singular).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5790')\">BDB5790</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5697')\">H5697</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5789')\">BDB5789</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5791')\">BDB5791</entry></div><p> I. <bdbheb>עֶגְלָה</bdbheb> <b>noun feminine</b> <highlightword>heifer</highlightword>; — absolute <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ע</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 15:9\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(1,15,9)\">Gen 15:9</ref> +; construct <bdbheb>עֶגְלַת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 7:21\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(23,7,21)\">Isa 7:21</ref> +; suffix <bdbheb>עֶגְלָתִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Judg 14:18\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(7,14,18)\">Judg 14:18</ref> plural construct <bdbheb>עֶגְלוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Hos 10:5\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(28,10,5)\">Hos 10:5</ref> (but see below); — <highlight>heifer</highlight>, <ref ref=\"Isa 7:21\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(23,7,21)\">Isa 7:21</ref>, used in ploughing <ref ref=\"Judg 14:18\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(7,14,18)\">Judg 14:18</ref> (figurative), threshing <ref ref=\"Jer 50:11\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"50\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"50\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(24,50,11)\">Jer 50:11</ref> (<bdbheb>דָשָׁא</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ע</bdbheb>, in simile, see  <bdbheb><reflink>דּוּשׁ</reflink></bdbheb>, read perhaps <bdbheb>דָשָׁה</bdbheb>), figurative of stateliness etc. <ref ref=\"Jer 46:20\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(24,46,20)\">Jer 46:20</ref> <bdbheb>מְלֻמָּדָה</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ע</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Hos 10:11\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(28,10,11)\">Hos 10:11</ref> <highlight>a trained heifer</highlight> (simile of Ephraim); used for sacrifice <ref ref=\"1Sam 16:2\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(9,16,2)\">1Sam 16:2</ref> (<bdbheb>עֶגְלַת בָּקָר</bdbheb>); cut in two for ratifying covenant <ref ref=\"Gen 15:9\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(1,15,9)\">Gen 15:9</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>; <bdbheb>מְשֻׁלֶּשֶׁת</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ע</bdbheb>; compare <bdbheb>עֵגֶל</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jer 34:18\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(24,34,18)\">Jer 34:18</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 34:19\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(24,34,19)\">Jer 34:19</ref>); in cleansing city from blood-guiltiness <ref ref=\"Deut 21:3\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(5,21,3)\">Deut 21:3</ref> (<bdbheb>בָּקָר</bdbheb>